1
00:00:08,980 --> 00:00:13,940
(This story is entirely fictional)

2
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:26,400
Mr. Wang.

3
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:28,800
How do you like this girl?

4
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:30,680
Pretty and sharp.

5
00:00:30,680 --> 00:00:33,400
(Based on the novel
Doctor Qin: Executer)

6
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:36,600
Quite a looker.

7
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:38,400
But

8
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,040
why is she so uptight?

9
00:00:42,750 --> 00:00:43,680
Come on.

10
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:45,400
It's her first time meeting you.

11
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:46,400
She's just a little shy.

12
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:47,440
It's normal.

13
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:49,200
Xue.

14
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:50,800
Come here.

15
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:00,480
I'm talking to you.

16
00:01:00,480 --> 00:01:01,840
You deaf or something?

17
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:04,640
Mr. Wang, don't mind her.

18
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:06,200
She's too young.

19
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:07,880
Naive. Never been around.

20
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:09,640
But she catches on quick.

21
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:10,600
She's smart.

22
00:01:11,240 --> 00:01:13,680
You can teach her a thing or two later.

23
00:01:13,680 --> 00:01:14,480
Yeah?

24
00:01:14,740 --> 00:01:15,380
Mm-hmm.

25
00:01:17,600 --> 00:01:18,400
Come here.

26
00:01:19,280 --> 00:01:20,840
Feed Mr. Wang a cherry.

27
00:01:26,120 --> 00:01:27,080
I said feed him!

28
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:28,360
Stop dragging your feet!

29
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:50,080
Wipe those cheap tears off your face.

30
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,640
Think about
your grandma's medical bills.

31
00:02:07,440 --> 00:02:09,160
Put away the fear

32
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:10,880
and the attitude.

33
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:15,680
Make that man in there feel like

34
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:17,880
he owns you,

35
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:21,400
and you'll get everything you want.

36
00:02:23,150 --> 00:02:27,310
♪Guess how many lives
I've lived through♪

37
00:02:27,840 --> 00:02:30,850
♪The fluorescent powder
tears the scars open♪

38
00:02:30,850 --> 00:02:33,690
♪Fresh blood feeds the crocodiles♪

39
00:02:34,420 --> 00:02:37,400
♪They stroll down the hallway
with smirks♪

40
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:42,160
♪When the prey breaks free,
the hunter masks up and runs♪

41
00:02:44,430 --> 00:02:48,250
♪Don't ask which hand
I settle scores with♪

42
00:02:48,250 --> 00:02:51,780
♪By the sunflowers,
the cat's eyes will lock on♪

43
00:02:51,780 --> 00:02:55,280
♪Their debts aren't written on paper♪

44
00:02:55,280 --> 00:02:59,620
♪Crocodile tears flow
as the feast begins♪

45
00:02:59,620 --> 00:03:02,060
(Fengshan Villa Secret Room)

46
00:03:02,710 --> 00:03:06,720
♪A cat has nine lives,
and keeps a tab on every single one♪

47
00:03:09,690 --> 00:03:13,570
♪A cat has nine lives,
and keeps a tab on every single one♪

48
00:03:22,220 --> 00:03:26,220
=Doctor Qin: Executer=
=Episode 2=

49
00:03:27,760 --> 00:03:28,720
You guessed right.

50
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:31,040
We found a high concentration
of a powerful hallucinogen

51
00:03:31,040 --> 00:03:32,000
in the blood

52
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,360
of the victim and the cat.

53
00:03:33,560 --> 00:03:34,240
Scopolamine.

54
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:36,040
Scopolamine?

55
00:03:36,280 --> 00:03:38,600
A powerful
central nervous system inhibitor.

56
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:39,600
Overuse

57
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:42,360
causes hallucinations, delirium,
respiratory depression,

58
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:43,720
even coma and death.

59
00:03:55,680 --> 00:03:56,960
That makes sense.

60
00:03:56,960 --> 00:03:59,720
The drug knocks you out fast
and loosens up the muscles.

61
00:03:59,920 --> 00:04:00,920
Perfectly explains

62
00:04:00,920 --> 00:04:02,880
why there were no signs of a struggle.

63
00:04:02,880 --> 00:04:04,160
And we found

64
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:05,560
some very fine particles

65
00:04:05,560 --> 00:04:08,120
in the residue
under Su Shi's fingernails.

66
00:04:08,120 --> 00:04:09,680
Microscopic and spectral analysis shows

67
00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:10,800
it's impatiens pollen

68
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:12,600
and some aged pine needle debris.

69
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:14,000
We also

70
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:15,320
found some particles

71
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:17,040
with a special fluorescent reaction.

72
00:04:17,240 --> 00:04:18,640
Still analyzing the composition.

73
00:04:18,760 --> 00:04:21,840
Impatiens pollen
and pine needles together?

74
00:04:22,320 --> 00:04:24,480
In Longfan, only two places
have both impatiens

75
00:04:24,480 --> 00:04:25,160
(Fengshan)
and pine forests.

76
00:04:25,400 --> 00:04:26,600
One is Qingshan Temple.

77
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:27,720
The other is Fengshan.

78
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:29,320
When I went hiking last year,

79
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:31,520
I heard the impatiens at Qingshan Temple

80
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:32,520
froze to death in winter.

81
00:04:32,520 --> 00:04:34,560
If Su Tang really drove that car away,

82
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:35,680
she's probably

83
00:04:35,880 --> 00:04:36,960
still up in Fengshan.

84
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:38,960
(Fengshan Flower Fields)

85
00:04:38,960 --> 00:04:40,800
Everyone, keep an eye out
for signs of human activity.

86
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:41,600
Stay safe.

87
00:04:41,640 --> 00:04:42,440
Search.

88
00:04:47,920 --> 00:04:48,840
All teams,

89
00:04:48,920 --> 00:04:50,320
report your status.

90
00:04:50,480 --> 00:04:52,280
(Team A found signs of recent activity)

91
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:53,400
(at an abandoned ranger station.)

92
00:04:53,640 --> 00:04:55,200
(Team B found fresh tire tracks)

93
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:56,040
(heading toward the cliff.)

94
00:04:56,720 --> 00:04:58,040
(Team C found clothing fragments)

95
00:04:58,040 --> 00:04:59,520
(that look like they were torn off.)

96
00:05:18,120 --> 00:05:19,800
Liang! Shiyu!

97
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:21,440
What did you find?

98
00:05:21,560 --> 00:05:22,360
Look!

99
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:26,100
(Fan A 71954)

100
00:05:28,480 --> 00:05:30,400
White powder on the driver's seat.

101
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:32,280
Dried porridge stains
on the passenger seat.

102
00:05:32,880 --> 00:05:35,320
Dried blood on the gear shift
and steering wheel.

103
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:38,360
The brake line's been tampered with.

104
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:40,520
Shiyu,

105
00:05:40,760 --> 00:05:42,160
did you check up there just now?

106
00:05:42,160 --> 00:05:43,200
Any brake marks?

107
00:05:43,200 --> 00:05:43,920
No.

108
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:45,920
What about you guys?

109
00:05:45,920 --> 00:05:47,000
- No.
- No.

110
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:49,440
(Liang, target spotted.)

111
00:05:49,520 --> 00:05:50,320
The exact position?

112
00:05:50,560 --> 00:05:51,800
(Six o'clock from the meetup point.)

113
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:52,600
(Four hundred meters.)

114
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:53,240
Move.

115
00:05:59,280 --> 00:06:00,000
Did you call 120?

116
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:01,080
Already on the way.

117
00:06:11,200 --> 00:06:12,200
She's still got a pulse.

118
00:06:17,360 --> 00:06:18,560
Multiple fractures all over.

119
00:06:18,560 --> 00:06:19,560
Hemorrhagic shock.

120
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:27,120
Fabric fibers?

121
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:28,840
Should we move her out first?

122
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:29,840
Don't touch her yet.

123
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:31,600
She might have a head injury.

124
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:32,600
Wait for 120.

125
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:34,720
And these scrapes

126
00:06:34,800 --> 00:06:36,960
could be from a violent struggle.

127
00:06:50,160 --> 00:06:51,400
Blood up there?

128
00:07:03,240 --> 00:07:05,920
Tiny jagged scratches
along the wound edges.

129
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:09,000
The jagged edges
match the wound perfectly.

130
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:11,800
Did the daughter really kill the mother?

131
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:19,080
Let me out!

132
00:07:19,080 --> 00:07:20,440
Let me die!

133
00:07:22,240 --> 00:07:24,040
Just let me die!

134
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:27,320
I want you to feel what it's like

135
00:07:27,320 --> 00:07:29,760
to be locked up, wishing you were dead!

136
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:30,280
Tang.

137
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:31,040
Open the door.

138
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:32,280
I'm your mom.

139
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:37,200
Didn't you love feeding them?

140
00:07:37,840 --> 00:07:38,640
Feed them.

141
00:07:38,880 --> 00:07:40,840
Let them taste you!

142
00:07:42,360 --> 00:07:43,960
The white powder residue
found in the car

143
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:45,240
tested positive for heroin.

144
00:07:45,360 --> 00:07:46,280
Now it all makes sense.

145
00:07:46,960 --> 00:07:49,160
Su Tang killed her mother, overdosed,

146
00:07:49,360 --> 00:07:50,120
hallucinated,

147
00:07:50,120 --> 00:07:51,760
and drove off the cliff.

148
00:07:51,800 --> 00:07:53,240
Killing her mother for drug money?

149
00:07:54,400 --> 00:07:55,880
And in such a brutal way.

150
00:07:55,880 --> 00:07:57,280
Could someone tripping on drugs

151
00:07:57,280 --> 00:07:58,920
really pull off something
that meticulous?

152
00:07:58,960 --> 00:07:59,760
And

153
00:08:00,640 --> 00:08:02,040
what about the gasoline traces
on the car,

154
00:08:02,360 --> 00:08:03,920
the faked lock-up,

155
00:08:03,920 --> 00:08:05,440
the professional lock-picking?

156
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:06,400
How do you explain those?

157
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:08,560
The wounds on Su Shi's body

158
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:10,280
were clean and steady.

159
00:08:10,520 --> 00:08:11,320
And the cuts

160
00:08:11,320 --> 00:08:13,480
precisely avoided all the major bones.

161
00:08:13,520 --> 00:08:14,280
This is definitely not

162
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:16,000
the work of someone
in a hallucinogenic frenzy.

163
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:17,920
The special restraint marks,

164
00:08:18,240 --> 00:08:19,520
the professional blade wounds,

165
00:08:19,640 --> 00:08:20,960
the hallucinogen,

166
00:08:21,320 --> 00:08:23,880
the staged scene, the cleanup...

167
00:08:24,040 --> 00:08:25,960
All point to a killer with serious

168
00:08:25,960 --> 00:08:27,960
counter-investigation skills
and nerves of steel.

169
00:08:28,040 --> 00:08:30,200
Someone in an extreme mental state
couldn't do that.

170
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:31,800
Su Tang

171
00:08:32,440 --> 00:08:33,880
is very likely just a decoy.

172
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:35,440
Mr. Dong.

173
00:08:37,160 --> 00:08:38,000
Take a look at this.

174
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:40,960
The nylon fibers on the seatbelt buckle

175
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:42,880
were corroded

176
00:08:42,880 --> 00:08:43,680
by industrial-strength alkali.

177
00:08:43,680 --> 00:08:45,320
Under normal conditions, it's fine.

178
00:08:45,440 --> 00:08:47,080
But under massive impact,

179
00:08:47,120 --> 00:08:48,160
like a car crash,

180
00:08:48,160 --> 00:08:49,960
it would snap before anything else.

181
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:51,080
You're saying

182
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:52,520
it was tampered with?

183
00:08:52,520 --> 00:08:53,440
There are

184
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:54,880
similar needle-prick leak points
on the brake line too.

185
00:08:54,920 --> 00:08:57,000
It would make the brakes fail slowly.

186
00:08:57,600 --> 00:08:58,960
Put those two together

187
00:08:58,960 --> 00:09:00,280
and it's a double safeguard.

188
00:09:00,280 --> 00:09:01,320
A guaranteed kill.

189
00:09:02,160 --> 00:09:04,400
That letter doesn't look like something
Su Tang could've written.

190
00:09:04,760 --> 00:09:06,560
I think this was

191
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:10,400
a planned, premeditated execution.

192
00:09:11,160 --> 00:09:12,280
I agree with Qin Ming.

193
00:09:13,160 --> 00:09:14,560
(Serving the People)
This kind of precision sabotage

194
00:09:14,560 --> 00:09:16,760
takes expertise and a calm mind.

195
00:09:16,760 --> 00:09:18,640
No way an addict could pull this off

196
00:09:18,640 --> 00:09:20,240
in a panic.

197
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:21,280
Sunflowers...

198
00:09:22,760 --> 00:09:24,000
What do they even mean?

199
00:09:27,460 --> 00:09:33,980
(Longfan Public Security Bureau
Forensic Identification Center)

200
00:09:38,860 --> 00:09:43,060
(Lab Report)

201
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:01,200
Hey, Xiao.

202
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:02,120
Qin?

203
00:10:02,680 --> 00:10:04,280
What made you think of me?

204
00:10:07,040 --> 00:10:08,440
Can you get in touch with Jin Keke?

205
00:10:08,880 --> 00:10:09,720
Jin Keke?

206
00:10:11,280 --> 00:10:12,880
Why ask about her all of a sudden?

207
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:14,960
Don't tell me
you're getting ideas again.

208
00:10:14,960 --> 00:10:16,240
Didn't get her in high school,

209
00:10:16,280 --> 00:10:17,720
so now you wanna try again?

210
00:10:17,920 --> 00:10:18,720
Cut it out.

211
00:10:19,320 --> 00:10:20,720
I just wanna know how she's doing.

212
00:10:21,040 --> 00:10:22,320
Alright.

213
00:10:22,320 --> 00:10:23,120
I'll cut it out.

214
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:25,160
I really don't have her contact.

215
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:26,880
Ever since that happened,

216
00:10:26,880 --> 00:10:28,120
she hasn't been the same person.

217
00:10:28,120 --> 00:10:29,280
Stopped talking to everyone.

218
00:10:29,680 --> 00:10:30,800
Then she moved away.

219
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:32,320
She doesn't even show up to reunions.

220
00:10:32,880 --> 00:10:33,800
I guess

221
00:10:34,680 --> 00:10:36,080
she doesn't wanna see
any of us ever again.

222
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:39,640
Qin,

223
00:10:40,200 --> 00:10:42,000
if you really wanna reach her,

224
00:10:42,200 --> 00:10:43,840
ask our class monitor.

225
00:10:43,960 --> 00:10:44,840
He knows people.

226
00:10:45,400 --> 00:10:46,240
Let's leave it there.

227
00:10:46,680 --> 00:10:47,680
I won't keep you from your hand.

228
00:11:02,240 --> 00:11:03,160
Why?

229
00:11:03,640 --> 00:11:04,760
Why are you doing this to me?

230
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:15,960
Stop looking at me like that!

231
00:11:16,680 --> 00:11:18,440
(Quit Addiction, Start Fresh)
Get out!

232
00:11:19,160 --> 00:11:20,920
The doctor said
her injuries are serious.

233
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:23,520
Multiple areas of brain damage.

234
00:11:23,920 --> 00:11:25,320
Plus a mild concussion.

235
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:26,480
Her left hand is broken.

236
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:27,960
The worst part is her addiction

237
00:11:27,960 --> 00:11:29,240
and her mental state.

238
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:32,040
Her whole body is defensive

239
00:11:32,040 --> 00:11:33,120
and full of self-denial.

240
00:11:33,440 --> 00:11:35,360
It's not like a normal withdrawal.

241
00:11:36,040 --> 00:11:39,440
More like a breakdown
after long-term mental abuse.

242
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:41,240
We can't get anything out of her.

243
00:11:41,960 --> 00:11:43,280
The moment she gets emotional,

244
00:11:43,960 --> 00:11:44,760
she starts saying

245
00:11:45,120 --> 00:11:46,840
stuff like dirty and liar.

246
00:11:47,520 --> 00:11:48,760
It makes no sense.

247
00:11:48,880 --> 00:11:50,880
This isn't just some random outburst.

248
00:11:51,040 --> 00:11:54,240
It's more like she's been fed
some kind of paranoid belief.

249
00:11:55,040 --> 00:11:57,640
She might be repeating
someone else's words.

250
00:11:58,280 --> 00:12:00,760
You're saying she was brainwashed?

251
00:12:03,100 --> 00:12:04,840
(Quit Addiction, Start Fresh)

252
00:12:04,840 --> 00:12:07,120
You asked me last time
about Su's strange behavior.

253
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:08,240
Something just came back to me.

254
00:12:08,280 --> 00:12:09,320
One night,

255
00:12:09,880 --> 00:12:10,720
I went back to grab my bag,

256
00:12:10,720 --> 00:12:12,440
and Su was sitting alone in the dark,

257
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:13,640
staring out the window.

258
00:12:14,280 --> 00:12:15,080
Su...

259
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:17,280
Li!

260
00:12:18,160 --> 00:12:20,240
I keep feeling like
there's a pair of eyes watching me.

261
00:12:29,360 --> 00:12:30,880
I've never seen Su scared.

262
00:12:30,880 --> 00:12:31,960
She grabbed my hand so hard

263
00:12:31,960 --> 00:12:33,720
her nails almost dug into my skin.

264
00:12:34,280 --> 00:12:35,640
Always remember the shame.

265
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:37,080
Always protect Tang.

266
00:12:39,960 --> 00:12:41,760
And that time her daughter
came asking for money.

267
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:43,640
This is it?

268
00:12:43,920 --> 00:12:45,160
You think I'm a beggar?

269
00:12:45,160 --> 00:12:46,880
Do you have any idea
what I'm dealing with?

270
00:12:46,920 --> 00:12:47,840
What are you dealing with?

271
00:12:47,840 --> 00:12:49,000
Rotting in the streets

272
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:50,160
like your deadbeat dad?

273
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:51,240
Here we go again.

274
00:12:51,800 --> 00:12:53,360
I paid for your rehab,

275
00:12:53,360 --> 00:12:55,440
not so you could come back
and be trash again.

276
00:12:55,760 --> 00:12:56,560
Yeah.

277
00:12:57,360 --> 00:12:58,520
I'm trash.

278
00:13:00,280 --> 00:13:01,240
So what about you?

279
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:03,320
Playing around with the guys‌...

280
00:13:03,320 --> 00:13:05,240
At least I know what I want!

281
00:13:06,120 --> 00:13:06,920
You?

282
00:13:07,560 --> 00:13:09,360
All you do is obey men

283
00:13:09,680 --> 00:13:10,880
and cling to them.

284
00:13:12,160 --> 00:13:13,760
So what if I cling to men?

285
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:15,560
You taught me that.

286
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:19,560
Even if you wanna be trash,

287
00:13:20,720 --> 00:13:22,520
don't be free trash.

288
00:13:23,600 --> 00:13:24,760
So I should be

289
00:13:25,040 --> 00:13:27,040
expensive trash like you?

290
00:13:27,040 --> 00:13:28,560
Then at least let me look
as put-together

291
00:13:28,560 --> 00:13:29,680
as you do.

292
00:13:29,840 --> 00:13:31,160
I wanna grow my hair long!

293
00:13:31,160 --> 00:13:32,640
I wanna wear dresses!

294
00:13:32,640 --> 00:13:33,920
What gives you the right to control me?

295
00:13:34,040 --> 00:13:35,600
These clothes are for adults,

296
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:37,440
not for little girls like you!

297
00:13:37,440 --> 00:13:38,360
I'm an adult now.

298
00:13:38,360 --> 00:13:39,720
You can't control me anymore!

299
00:13:41,240 --> 00:13:42,440
I warned you

300
00:13:43,880 --> 00:13:45,880
to stay away from those filthy men.

301
00:13:47,040 --> 00:13:49,360
You're with them all the time.

302
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:50,680
And you're telling me what to do?

303
00:13:52,920 --> 00:13:54,120
I get it.

304
00:13:55,080 --> 00:13:56,440
You think

305
00:13:56,600 --> 00:13:57,600
you're the only one

306
00:13:57,680 --> 00:13:59,840
who gets to be with men,

307
00:14:00,040 --> 00:14:01,040
and I can't, right?

308
00:14:01,680 --> 00:14:02,440
Exactly.

309
00:14:03,080 --> 00:14:04,920
Anyone can, but not you!

310
00:14:04,920 --> 00:14:05,760
Why not?

311
00:14:06,640 --> 00:14:08,520
Because your deadbeat dad

312
00:14:08,520 --> 00:14:10,760
was an animal
who couldn't control himself.

313
00:14:11,560 --> 00:14:12,560
And you're the same.

314
00:14:13,080 --> 00:14:15,760
You've got the same filthy blood
running through your veins.

315
00:14:19,160 --> 00:14:20,240
You're calling me...

316
00:14:21,480 --> 00:14:23,040
You're calling me filthy?

317
00:14:24,040 --> 00:14:26,840
Half the blood in my body
comes from you.

318
00:14:26,960 --> 00:14:29,040
Why don't you talk
about how filthy your own blood is?

319
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:34,800
Tang,

320
00:14:37,600 --> 00:14:39,080
I'm helping you.

321
00:14:41,200 --> 00:14:43,640
So those men don't chew you up

322
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:45,480
and spit you out with nothing left.

323
00:14:47,560 --> 00:14:48,560
Well, thanks a lot.

324
00:14:49,400 --> 00:14:50,520
(Su didn't cry that day.)

325
00:14:50,520 --> 00:14:52,240
(She just sat there,
staring at the door.)

326
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:53,520
(Her eyes were scarily hollow.)

327
00:14:53,840 --> 00:14:55,520
(Su really did love her daughter.)

328
00:14:55,720 --> 00:14:56,680
That's not love.

329
00:14:58,200 --> 00:14:59,080
That's a chain.

330
00:15:05,240 --> 00:15:06,080
Okay.

331
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:07,800
Mr. Han.

332
00:15:08,040 --> 00:15:09,720
Su Tang's doing better now.

333
00:15:10,280 --> 00:15:11,280
We can question her.

334
00:15:28,300 --> 00:15:34,370
(Quit Addiction, Start fresh)

335
00:15:35,560 --> 00:15:36,360
Su Tang,

336
00:15:37,960 --> 00:15:40,480
did your mother have any enemies?

337
00:15:42,120 --> 00:15:43,240
Enemies?

338
00:15:46,880 --> 00:15:48,440
If we're talking enemies,

339
00:15:50,280 --> 00:15:53,080
the person
who hates her most in this world

340
00:15:53,680 --> 00:15:55,440
is probably me.

341
00:15:58,280 --> 00:16:00,440
She locked me up.

342
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:03,240
With chains

343
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:05,600
and a cage.

344
00:16:07,720 --> 00:16:08,880
And she said

345
00:16:09,640 --> 00:16:11,120
she was helping me get clean.

346
00:16:12,640 --> 00:16:14,680
But she was just scared
I'd steal her man!

347
00:16:15,160 --> 00:16:15,960
Man?

348
00:16:16,640 --> 00:16:18,000
What man are you talking about?

349
00:16:18,360 --> 00:16:19,200
What's his name?

350
00:16:21,440 --> 00:16:22,680
Zhang Xiaodong.

351
00:16:24,600 --> 00:16:26,640
She let danger into our home.

352
00:16:28,240 --> 00:16:29,800
He got bored of her,

353
00:16:31,480 --> 00:16:33,840
so he set his sights on me.

354
00:16:37,160 --> 00:16:39,120
And got me hooked on drugs.

355
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:45,640
Qin Ming.

356
00:16:46,320 --> 00:16:47,440
I heard you were looking for me.

357
00:16:48,400 --> 00:16:49,240
What do you need?

358
00:17:02,280 --> 00:17:06,630
♪Sunset washes over the old wall♪

359
00:17:07,030 --> 00:17:11,380
♪Milk tea cools on the stone steps♪

360
00:17:11,380 --> 00:17:15,540
♪Sea wind tugs at your sleeve♪

361
00:17:15,860 --> 00:17:19,790
♪Unspoken words just flee and fade♪

362
00:17:28,740 --> 00:17:32,630
♪The marks on the desk
have faded yellow♪

363
00:17:32,630 --> 00:17:35,630
♪I turned around,
and a gunshot rang out♪

364
00:17:36,100 --> 00:17:39,740
♪No one can truly feel another's pain♪

365
00:17:39,740 --> 00:17:43,990
♪The wind is cold,
a fading shadow sways♪

366
00:17:43,990 --> 00:17:48,700
♪Tonight, I don't care
about the universe♪

367
00:17:48,700 --> 00:17:53,130
♪I only want to see this through
with you♪

368
00:17:53,710 --> 00:17:57,490
♪A bullet pierces the spring night♪

369
00:17:57,490 --> 00:18:01,810
♪You sink into the vast crowd♪

370
00:18:10,540 --> 00:18:14,750
♪Years later, when we meet again♪

371
00:18:14,750 --> 00:18:19,080
♪Don't mention this moonlit night♪

372
00:18:19,080 --> 00:18:22,870
♪The waves smooth
two lines of footprints♪

373
00:18:22,870 --> 00:18:25,760
♪Half a cup of sweetness
sinks into the sand♪

374
00:18:25,760 --> 00:18:30,570
♪Tonight, I don't care
about the universe♪

375
00:18:30,570 --> 00:18:35,230
♪I only want to see this through
with you♪

376
00:18:35,230 --> 00:18:37,510
♪Wind back to shore,
clouds back to hills♪

377
00:18:37,510 --> 00:18:39,590
♪We stop here in this night♪

378
00:18:39,590 --> 00:18:44,020
♪This is the past, the only,
the last look back♪

379
00:18:44,020 --> 00:18:50,010
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

380
00:18:52,470 --> 00:18:58,910
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

381
00:19:10,290 --> 00:19:17,280
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

382
00:19:19,470 --> 00:19:25,390
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪
